<title>UK: TI wins $200 mln orders from Boeing.</title>
<headline>TI wins $200 mln orders from Boeing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group TI Group Plc said on Monday its Dowty Aerospace and Messier Dowty divisions had won contracts worth over $200 milllion for the Bell Boeing 609 Tiltrotor aircraft.</p>
<p>TI said the deals, to supply fly-by-wire flight control actuators and associated test rig, and landing gear systems wil be worth in excess of $100 million each to Dowty Aerospace and Messier-Dowty over the life of the programme.</p>
<p>The Bell Boeing 609 is the world's first commercial tiltrotor aircraft and is aimed at corporate resource development and emergency medical markets, TI said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
